Enhancement: More flexible formats for backup and rewrite time related options

Restic backup --time allowed in the past only the format "2006-01-02 15:04:05".

``backup --time`` and ``rewrite --new-time`` can now use the following range of time
formats. The time part "HH:MM:SS" is optional. If left away, "00:00:00" is assumed:
y-m-d HH:MM:SS
d.m.y HH:MM:SS

with additional modifiers for timezone name and timezone offset
y-m-d HH:MM:SS MST
y-m-d HH:MM:SS -0700

d.m.y HH:MM:SS MST
d.m.y HH:MM:SS -0700

